{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Dm7] | [Cm7] |
| [Ebmaj7] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]When the night is [Dm7]long and the morning's slow [Cm7]to come
[Bb]When the news is [Dm7]hard and my heart is go[Cm7]ing numb
I can't see the [Gm7]whole design, I [Dm7]only hold a thread
But I'm [Ebmaj7]standing on the word the a[Eb/F]postle Paul once said
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
And we [Bb]know that in [Dm7]all things
God [Cm7]works for the good of those who love him
Who are [Bb]called according to his [Dm7]purpose
In all [Cm7]things, in all [Eb]things
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Every closing door [Dm7]and every winding [Cm7]road
[Bb]Every empty chair [Dm7]and every heavy [Cm7]load
The God who [Gm7]gave his Son for me will [Dm7]not forget me now
So [Ebmaj7]I lay down every worry and [Eb/F]I let my spirit bow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
And we [Bb]know that in [Dm7]all things
God [Cm7]works for the good of those who love him
Who are [Bb]called according to his [Dm7]purpose
In all [Cm7]things, in all [Ebmaj7]things
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm7]If God is for us, who can be a[Ebmaj7]gainst us
Who will sepa[Bb]rate us from the love of [Gm7]Christ
In all these things [Dm7]we are more than [Cm7]conquerors
Through [F7sus4]him who loved us
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Neither death nor life
[Dm7]Nor anything else in [Cm7]all creation
[Bb]Will be able [Dm7]to separate us
From the [Cm7]love of God that is in Christ Jesus [Bb]our Lord
{end_of_verse}
